    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d666">

                <pb facs="0678" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.504/363: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dickerson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-29T14:00:00+03:00">December 29, 1941—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2109. With reference to the decree of June 26, 1940,<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d666-f1"/> forbidding all workers in Soviet factories and
                    enterprises to leave their employment without permission, under penalty of
                    imprisonment of from 2 to 4 months, the local press has published a decree dated
                    December 26, 1941, raising the penalty for “arbitrary departure” of workers in
                    armaments <pb facs="0679" n="667" xml:id="pg667"/> and related industries to
                    from 5 to 8 years and giving jurisdiction in such cases to court martial. The
                    present decree applies not only to ordinary factories but also to those which
                    have been evacuated. Thus workers in armament plants evacuated to the east are
                    obliged to move with the plant to its new location.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dickerson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d666-f1" n="40" xml:id="d666-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 760, June 27, 1940, from the Chargé in the Soviet Union, <ref
                        target="frus1940v03#pg_202">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1940, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, p. 202</ref>.</p>
